## Context

Items C, D, E, I, J from ticket 0071 triage. All cosmetic except E (one helper
function). No logic changes. Item H (built: line) is already resolved by PR #80
(vcsRevision present → built: line shown; absent → omitted).

- C (`check.go`): `WARNING %s:` → `WARN %s:` — standardize to shorter prefix
  used by the stray-source warning added in PR #79.
- D (`close.go`): `ALREADY_CLOSED` → `CLOSED (already)` — matches
  `PASS (3 tickets, 2 warnings)` style; no underscores in status verbs.
- E (`check.go`, `validate.go`): `(s)` fake pluralization →
  `plural(n int, word string) string` helper; `"1 file"` vs `"2 files"`.
- I (`init.go`): `%t` boolean → `yes`/`no`; "pointer" → "entry";
  `"manifest: %s"` → `"manifest written: %s"`.
- J (`validate.go`): `"preamble"` → `"header section"` in error messages
  (2 occurrences).

## Actions

1. `check.go`: change `"WARNING %s:"` format verb to `"WARN %s:"` (2 strings).
2. `close.go`: change `"ALREADY_CLOSED"` to `"CLOSED (already)"`.
3. Add `func plural(n int, word string) string` — returns `"1 word"` or `"N words"`.
   Place in `util.go` (create if absent) or inline in `check.go`.
4. `check.go`: replace `"%d warning(s)"` format with `plural(n, "warning")`.
5. `validate.go`: replace `"PASS (%d file(s))"` with `plural(n, "file")` variant.
6. `init.go`: replace `%t` with `yes`/`no` ternary; `"AGENTS.md pointer"` →
   `"AGENTS.md entry"`; `"manifest: %s"` → `"manifest written: %s"`.
7. `validate.go`: replace both occurrences of `"preamble"` with `"header section"`.

## Test

Extend `tests/test_check.sh`: 1 warning → `"1 warning"` (not `"1 warning(s)"`);
2 warnings → `"2 warnings"`.

Extend `tests/test_validate.sh`: 1 file → `"1 file"`; 2 files → `"2 files"`.

Extend `tests/test_close.sh`: already-closed ticket outputs `CLOSED (already)`.

Extend `tests/test_init.sh`: output contains `yes` or `no`, not `true`/`false`;
contains `manifest written:`; contains `AGENTS.md entry`.

## Exit criteria

- `make test` passes.
- No `WARNING ` (with trailing space) in `check.go`.
- No `ALREADY_CLOSED` anywhere in source.
- No `(s)` pluralization in format strings.
- No `preamble` in `validate.go` error messages.
- No `%t` in `init.go` output format strings.
